[?2004l252: ## Investigation Brief 02 — Status Precedence
253: 
254: Auditor directive (mandatory for extract):
255: 
256: Interview notes with the compliance desk confirmed status fights between mail,
257: amendments, and corrections. Ledger rows provide the base status (lowercase on
258: output). Status precedence from lowest to highest is: pending, approved,
259: rejected, reversed. Email excerpts may change status only when the From line
260: contains `compliance@` anywhere in the address; ignore all other senders.
261: 
[?2004hroot@796178391c5a:/app# sed -n '1,240p' /tmp/brief03_only.txt
[?2004l468: ## Investigation Brief 03 — Compliance Mail Timing
469: 
470: Extract policy (authoritative):
471: 
472: The March mail-room audit explained missing holds: agents applied compliance
473: messages without checking dispatch dates. When an excerpt includes
474: `sent: YYYY-MM-DD`, apply the status change only if sent is greater than or
475: equal to the ledger date for that transaction. When no `sent:` line is present,
476: apply the status change if precedence allows. Correction notices always apply
477: after ledger rows, meeting amendments, and mail excerpts have been merged.
478: 
[?2004hroot@796178391c5a:/app# sed -n '1,260p' /tmp/brief04_only.txt
[?2004l685: ## Investigation Brief 04 — Correction Notice Precedence
686: 
687: Controller memo (binding reconciliation rule):
688: 
689: The corrections desk ships multiple notices per field. When several notices
690: target the same transaction and field, the notice with the lexicographically
691: greatest `effective` date wins. For each winning notice, `previous_value` in
692: `reconciliation_report.jsonl` is the field value immediately before that notice
693: applies (after ledger, amendments, and emails). Owner corrections override
694: both ledger owners and signed meeting amendments when applied in this step.
695: 
[?2004hroot@796178391c5a:/app# sed -n '1,260p' /tmp/brief05_only.txt
[?2004l828: ## Investigation Brief 05 — Meeting Amendments and Owners
829: 
830: Committee ruling (binding for extract):
831: 
832: Committee minutes show owner churn from unsigned drafts. Ledger owner is the
833: default. Meeting note amendments under `#### Amendment for TXN-<uuid>` replace
834: owner when `signed: true` (case insensitive) and, when the amendment includes
835: `effective: YYYY-MM-DD`, only if that date is greater than or equal to the
836: ledger date for the transaction.
837: 
[?2004hroot@796178391c5a:/app# sed -n '1,260p' /tmp/brief09_only.txt
[?2004l1670: ## Investigation Brief 09 — Mid-Year Amendment
1671: 
1672: Committee ruling (binding for extract):
1673: 
1674: Mid-year QA found compliance holds disappearing after date corrections. This
1675: amendment supersedes any earlier wording about hold timing. For `compliance_hold`
1676: only, compare each qualifying email's `sent:` date against the transaction's
1677: ledger date immediately before correction notices are applied — that is, the date
1678: in effect after ledger load, meeting amendments, and compliance mail merges, but
1679: before any correction notice changes `date` or `status`. Brief 03 still governs
1680: mail-driven status changes; this amendment governs only the hold flag.
1681: 
